  "finding": "Relocating a bottom contact without extending its original root leaves a local vertical void. Source-grid collision masks can erase a legal independently sliced root. A footprint crossing model steps requires separate visible surface contacts; succeeding paths require native height modulation over those contacts, including ordered hollow-wall collections.",
  "preservation": "Native support/interface patterns, roles and widths are retained. Model, Brim, and paths at/above 2.40 mm are unchanged within 0.002 mm output precision. No G-code instructions were edited. The original Release data_dir is used; no alternative configuration directory, install, commit or push is created.",
  "limitations": [
    "Gap evidence uses printed model slice surfaces and extrusion bottoms, not hardware measurements.",
    "31 organic/tree-bridge cases and this project do not establish correctness on every possible model.",
    "Parsed path counts include height/width fragments and do not count only independent trunk contours."
  ],
